        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "eacc089c-b65e-5467-80c5-38ab7f7118c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francis Keogh Gleason, Rocky Graziano\n- Organizations: MGM Studios, Academy Awards\n- Films: Somebody Up There Likes Me, An American in Paris, The Bad and the Beautiful, Gigi\n- Roles: Set decorator\n\nFacts:\n- Francis Keogh Gleason was born on April 14, 1906, and died on December 18, 1982.\n- Francis Keogh Gleason worked as a resident set decorator at MGM Studios for more than 40 years.\n- Francis Keogh Gleason won Academy Awards for An American in Paris in 1951 and for The Bad and the Beautiful in 1952.\n- Somebody Up There Likes Me is a 1956 American drama film based on the life of middleweight boxing legend Rocky Graziano.\n- Francis Keogh Gleason won Academy Awards for Somebody Up There Likes Me in 1956 and for Gigi in 1958.\n- Francis Keogh Gleason received three additional Academy Award nominations beyond his four wins.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "67a4ee16-c72b-5d9a-91a5-1786a7d93e0b",
